to make the attempt,

514
00:21:32,825 --> 00:21:33,927
you can certainly
have permission.

515
00:21:33,927 --> 00:21:35,362
How soon can you start?

516
00:21:35,362 --> 00:21:36,563
- Right away.

517
00:21:36,563 --> 00:21:37,763
The rocket ship is
all fueled and ready.

518
00:21:37,763 --> 00:21:38,698
Joan, call--

519
00:21:38,698 --> 00:21:39,900
- [Crow] The rocket ship?

520
00:21:39,900 --> 00:21:41,635
We are going back to
the moon it sound like.

521
00:21:41,635 --> 00:21:43,137
- [Joel] Terrific.
- I want to get started

522
00:21:43,137 --> 00:21:45,138
before there's any chance
of the news leaking out.

523
00:21:45,138 --> 00:21:49,375
So Reddick will be laying
for us when we get there.

524
00:21:50,510 --> 00:21:53,947
- [Joel] Watch the
scene everybody, whoops.

525
00:21:53,947 --> 00:21:56,450
- [Crow] Scarecrow, I think
I'll miss you most of all.

526
00:21:56,450 --> 00:21:58,418
- Hope this trip is as
easy as your last one.

527
00:21:58,418 --> 00:21:59,652
- Thanks.
It should be.

528
00:21:59,652 --> 00:22:00,820
- [Tom] Since we're
using the same footage.

529
00:22:00,820 --> 00:22:02,755
- Goodbye.
- Goodbye sir.

530
00:22:05,258 --> 00:22:07,260
- [Joel] You know, they should
invest in the control tower.

531
00:22:07,260 --> 00:22:08,662
- Hurry folks, here we go again.

532
00:22:08,662 --> 00:22:10,063
- All right.
All set.

533
00:22:10,063 --> 00:22:11,130
Any time now.

534
00:22:15,268 --> 00:22:18,038
(dramatic music)

535
00:22:26,413 --> 00:22:27,647
- Safety belt persons.

536
00:22:27,647 --> 00:22:30,150
- [Crow] No, it's not a law yet.

537
00:22:30,150 --> 00:22:31,552
- Fire power jet.

538
00:22:32,985 --> 00:22:34,755
- [Tom] Oh wonderful!

539
00:22:36,222 --> 00:22:37,323
- Fire main jets.

540
00:22:37,323 --> 00:22:38,258
- [Crow] Fire up all the jets.

541
00:22:38,258 --> 00:22:40,860
Get the Asmens back on contract.

542
00:22:44,663 --> 00:22:46,500
- [Joel] This thing's
loaded with candy.

543
00:22:46,500 --> 00:22:48,835
Watch what I can do with it.

544
00:22:50,737 --> 00:22:53,407
(air whooshing)

545
00:22:57,577 --> 00:23:00,013
You know I could
get used to this.

546
00:23:00,013 --> 00:23:01,415
- [Tom] Yes, yes.

547
00:23:03,283 --> 00:23:07,087
- [Joel] Cruising around
in a big jet, lots of beer.

548
00:23:07,087 --> 00:23:08,788
- We're 12 feet high.

549
00:23:08,788 --> 00:23:09,890
Set a course for the moon.

550
00:23:09,890 --> 00:23:11,958
- [Tom] Which moon?

551
00:23:11,958 --> 00:23:14,293
- [Crow] Take a left at
L2, you can't miss it.

552
00:23:14,293 --> 00:23:16,897
Dave's van is parked out front.

553
00:23:18,298 --> 00:23:19,732
- [Joel] Let me show you
what this baby can do.

554
00:23:19,732 --> 00:23:21,802
You guys ever seen
a barrel roll?

555
00:23:21,802 --> 00:23:22,702
(Joel laughs)

556
00:23:22,702 --> 00:23:23,970
- [Crow] Yikes.

557
00:23:25,072 --> 00:23:27,807
(dramatic music)

558
00:23:34,280 --> 00:23:35,848
- [Crow] That's it.

559
00:23:37,050 --> 00:23:38,318
If I'd have brought
that straight edge,

560
00:23:38,318 --> 00:23:40,620
we'd make it to the
moon at half the time.

561
00:23:40,620 --> 00:23:43,823
- [Joel] Here, use
my forehead's Phill.

562
00:23:46,092 --> 00:23:48,093
- We're just about here.

563
00:23:51,732 --> 00:23:54,902
We ought be down in
another two hours.

564
00:23:56,737 --> 00:23:59,807
(jet roaring)

565
00:23:59,807 --> 00:24:01,040
- [Tom] I'm really,
really hungry.

566
00:24:01,040 --> 00:24:03,543
Everyone looked
for the Stuckey's.

567
00:24:04,443 --> 00:24:06,378
- I can see the city now.

568
00:24:06,378 --> 00:24:09,715
We don't wanna get too close
to the spring West (mumbling)

569
00:24:09,715 --> 00:24:10,550
- Okay.

570
00:24:11,518 --> 00:24:14,020
(jet roaring)

571
00:24:17,290 --> 00:24:19,192
- [Crow] I see a
thousand points of light,

572
00:24:19,192 --> 00:24:20,660
it looks like Cleveland.

573
00:24:20,660 --> 00:24:22,395
- I'll take her down.

574
00:24:26,398 --> 00:24:28,100
- [Tom] We are now
approaching the moon.

575
00:24:28,100 --> 00:24:30,703
Please place your office
chairs to the upright position.

576
00:24:30,703 --> 00:24:33,573
The temperature on the
moon is a balmy 70 degrees.

577
00:24:33,573 --> 00:24:35,075
Enjoy your stay.

578
00:24:35,075 --> 00:24:37,510
- All right settle her down.

579
00:24:37,510 --> 00:24:39,712
- [Joel] It kinda looks
like the upper Dells.

580
00:24:39,712 --> 00:24:40,880
- [Crow] Yeah.

581
00:24:43,115 --> 00:24:46,887
- [Tom] Wisconsin is a
beautiful place to be.

582
00:24:48,322 --> 00:24:49,923
- You're sure you don't
want me to go alone?

583
00:24:49,923 --> 00:24:51,123
- No, not this time.

584
00:24:51,123 --> 00:24:52,825
This is just a scouting
trip to try to find

585
00:24:52,825 --> 00:24:54,160
where they keep the little Mary.

586
00:24:54,160 --> 00:24:55,462
- How do you expect to do that?

587
00:24:55,462 --> 00:24:56,663
- Well if I'm lucky,

588
00:24:56,663 --> 00:24:57,730
I'll be able to capture
one of the moon men

589
00:24:57,730 --> 00:24:59,632
and get some
information out of him.

590
00:24:59,632 --> 00:25:01,067
- [Crow] Well, bundle up honey.

591
00:25:01,067 --> 00:25:02,735
It's cold out there.

592
00:25:12,412 --> 00:25:14,147
- [Tom] Oh, radishes!

593
00:25:21,420 --> 00:25:23,990
- [Joel] Good morning,
where's my paper?

594
00:25:23,990 --> 00:25:25,192
Where's our shrubs?

595
00:25:25,192 --> 00:25:28,862
Oh, I'm on the moon,
how silly of me.

596
00:25:28,862 --> 00:25:29,963
Space travel.

597
00:25:31,063 --> 00:25:32,465
And away.

598
00:25:32,465 --> 00:25:35,902
(air whooshing)

599
00:25:35,902 --> 00:25:38,137
So sunny on the moon today.

600
00:25:41,775 --> 00:25:45,412
- [Joel] I'm just standing on
this hill and looking around.

601
00:25:45,412 --> 00:25:46,580
Oh, there I am.

602
00:25:46,580 --> 00:25:49,148
(Crow mumbles)

603
00:25:52,018 --> 00:25:54,587
- [Crow] Give me
that gun, it's mine.

604
00:25:54,587 --> 00:25:57,323
(dramatic music)

605
00:26:02,328 --> 00:26:05,998
- [Joel] Oh, it's that
old sea hunt routine.

606
00:26:07,533 --> 00:26:10,270
(dramatic music)

607
00:26:12,205 --> 00:26:17,210
- [Crow] (mumbles), what are
you trying to do, kill me?

608
00:26:18,345 --> 00:26:20,513
- Do you want me to cut
off your hair again?

609
00:26:20,513 --> 00:26:22,082
- No.

610
00:26:22,082 --> 00:26:23,015
No.

611
00:26:23,015 --> 00:26:24,683
- Where is the lunarian stored?

612
00:26:24,683 --> 00:26:26,185
- I will tell you.

613
00:26:27,553 --> 00:26:28,488
- Think I'll pass.

614
00:26:28,488 --> 00:26:29,957
- Sure you'll pass all right.

615
00:26:29,957 --> 00:26:31,323
- [Joel] Look they are forcing
him to eat Jones cooking.

616
00:26:31,323 --> 00:26:32,858
- He wasn't in any
position to lie very well.

617
00:26:32,858 --> 00:26:34,727
- No he was just getting his
free continental breakfast.

618
00:26:34,727 --> 00:26:36,195
- I think they are one of the
men who got the lunarian--

619
00:26:36,195 --> 00:26:37,997
- [Crow] I can't believe we're
trying to annihilate you.

620
00:26:37,997 --> 00:26:39,132
This is delicious.

621
00:26:39,132 --> 00:26:41,367
Hey pass the jam, will you?

622
00:26:47,507 --> 00:26:49,542
- It's a little after
nine, I'll go right in.

623
00:26:49,542 --> 00:26:51,945
You find a place to hide and
watch for me to come out.

624
00:26:51,945 --> 00:26:53,480
- Okay.

625
00:26:53,480 --> 00:26:55,082
- Cheesy, got rights through
their rigid security system.

626
00:26:55,082 --> 00:26:56,415
I can't believe that.

627
00:26:56,415 --> 00:26:58,818
(soft music)

628
00:27:08,995 --> 00:27:10,663
- About time you got here.

629
00:27:10,663 --> 00:27:11,998
- I was delayed.

630
00:27:14,000 --> 00:27:17,037
- [Tom] I'm a phony, you know.

631
00:27:17,037 --> 00:27:19,405
(soft music)

632
00:27:24,143 --> 00:27:26,680
- [Crow] Oh, that's right,
the sauna closes after 10.

633
00:27:26,680 --> 00:27:31,517
Well, I'll have to use my
my after-hours passkey.

634
00:27:31,517 --> 00:27:34,020
(door creaks)

635
00:27:41,127 --> 00:27:44,163
- [Joel] Ooh right,
I found my Nintendo.

636
00:27:44,163 --> 00:27:45,465
I'm gonna play
Super Mario Brothers

637
00:27:45,465 --> 00:27:49,135
and everything is gonna
be so great, oh Ted.

638
00:27:55,007 --> 00:27:57,710
(door creaking)

639
00:27:59,845 --> 00:28:01,447
- [Crow] Oh, I'm not
sorry for that one.

640
00:28:01,447 --> 00:28:03,015
That felt wonderful.

641
00:28:03,015 --> 00:28:04,583
(Crow coughs)

642
00:28:04,583 --> 00:28:06,485
Oh, I shouldn't do
that in a pressure suit

643
00:28:06,485 --> 00:28:08,988
(Crow coughs)

644
00:28:10,757 --> 00:28:12,492
- You got it.
- Yes.

645
00:28:12,492 --> 00:28:13,993
It's so heavy it's
going to take us a week

646
00:28:13,993 --> 00:28:16,595
to log it back to the ship.

647
00:28:16,595 --> 00:28:18,330
- Get outside, quick.

648
00:28:25,772 --> 00:28:28,608
- [Crow] These moon men
have used this for plywood,

649
00:28:28,608 --> 00:28:31,310
we haven't even dreamed of yet.

650
00:28:31,310 --> 00:28:33,947
(dramatic music)

651
00:28:33,947 --> 00:28:35,182
- [Crow] You wait in the car,

652
00:28:35,182 --> 00:28:36,950
I'm gonna go see
if Judy is ready.

653
00:28:36,950 --> 00:28:39,718
(dramatic music)

654
00:28:45,392 --> 00:28:46,225
- Come on.

655
00:28:50,830 --> 00:28:53,667
- [Joel] Judy, I'm down at
the lobby, can you buzz me up?

656
00:28:53,667 --> 00:28:55,067
We got dad's car.

657
00:28:56,735 --> 00:28:59,472
(dramatic music)

658
00:29:01,607 --> 00:29:03,743
Well Kesa Mou said no curfew.

659
00:29:03,743 --> 00:29:07,913
This is going to be the
best road trip ever.

660
00:29:07,913 --> 00:29:09,415
- [Crow] Here's the
lesson for you teens.

661
00:29:09,415 --> 00:29:11,550
Always lock up
and take the keys.

662
00:29:11,550 --> 00:29:13,587
Don't let a good boy go bad.

663
00:29:13,587 --> 00:29:14,587
- Very well.

664
00:29:22,262 --> 00:29:24,597
- [Crow] Ooh dad's
going to be torqued.

665
00:29:24,597 --> 00:29:26,632
I gotta make up a story.

666
00:29:26,632 --> 00:29:28,568
I Wandered to the far
side, yeah that's it.

667
00:29:28,568 --> 00:29:32,572
- Somebody stole my car,
send another one quickly.

668
00:29:32,572 --> 00:29:34,407
- [Joel] Listen, I'm not
gonna bail you out of trouble

669
00:29:34,407 --> 00:29:35,608
every time you lose a car.

670
00:29:35,608 --> 00:29:38,512
Someday I'm not gonna
be there for you.

671
00:29:38,512 --> 00:29:39,412
Yeah.

672
00:29:39,412 --> 00:29:42,082
- How the hill pressure?

673
00:29:42,082 --> 00:29:43,415
- It seems okay.

674
00:29:46,552 --> 00:29:48,722
- [Joel] This is so great.

675
00:29:51,190 --> 00:29:53,325
- [Tom] What those
dupe boys didn't know

676
00:29:53,325 --> 00:29:57,097
is that boss Hog had
stolen the general lead.

677
00:30:12,445 --> 00:30:14,880
(Ted mumbling)

678
00:30:14,880 --> 00:30:16,048
- There he is.

679
00:30:17,983 --> 00:30:19,418
That's right for an near miss.

680
00:30:19,418 --> 00:30:21,087
That might stop him.

681
00:30:24,423 --> 00:30:25,558
- What was that?

682
00:30:25,558 --> 00:30:26,692
- A ray gun blast.

683
00:30:26,692 --> 00:30:28,895
See what's behind us.

684
00:30:28,895 --> 00:30:31,563
- [Joel] I think it's a ray gun.

685
00:30:34,133 --> 00:30:35,402
[Crow] Oh, it's just some car.

686
00:30:35,402 --> 00:30:38,137
That must be, they
want to pass us.

687
00:30:38,137 --> 00:30:39,638
- There is another
car chasing us.

688
00:30:39,638 --> 00:30:40,940
We better use our gun.

689
00:30:40,940 --> 00:30:42,708
- We'll have to turn
around to do it.

690
00:30:42,708 --> 00:30:44,577
There is a bunch rocks that
will give us some shelter.

691
00:30:44,577 --> 00:30:46,212
We'll wait until we get there.

692
00:30:46,212 --> 00:30:48,915
(dramatic music)

693
00:30:52,252 --> 00:30:55,755
- It's heading for some
rocks, we'll have to stop.

694
00:30:55,755 --> 00:30:58,290
(ray gunblast)

695
00:30:59,792 --> 00:31:02,162
- [Joel] Oh, it's the Das
Boot theme all over again.

696
00:31:02,162 --> 00:31:04,097
(mumbling)

697
00:31:04,097 --> 00:31:05,163
- We're stuck.

698
00:31:05,163 --> 00:31:06,332
How say we are?

699
00:31:06,332 --> 00:31:08,033
- Pressure is down to nothing.

700
00:31:08,033 --> 00:31:09,468
I can fix this if I have time.

701
00:31:09,468 --> 00:31:13,205
- [Tom] I took moon
mechanics in high school.

702
00:31:15,608 --> 00:31:17,043
- Stop behind the rock.

703
00:31:17,043 --> 00:31:19,278
But I think I can blast it.

704
00:31:23,515 --> 00:31:26,585
(ray gun blasting)

705
00:31:26,585 --> 00:31:30,890
- [Joel] By this time my
lungs were aching for air.

706
00:31:30,890 --> 00:31:33,092
- [Crow] You hit the helium.

707
00:31:33,092 --> 00:31:35,160
- [Tom] Help me, help me.

708
00:31:36,062 --> 00:31:37,463
Oh no.

709
00:31:37,463 --> 00:31:40,232
(dramatic music)

710
00:31:45,738 --> 00:31:48,407
(doors closing)

711
00:31:54,747 --> 00:31:56,215
Okay Ted, stop here.

712
00:31:56,215 --> 00:31:59,685
I'm gonna hover here for a
moment and survey the landscape.

713
00:31:59,685 --> 00:32:01,520
Okay, now I think I'm gonna
fly over to that window

714
00:32:01,520 --> 00:32:04,023
and look for all those rotten
radar men from the moon.

715
00:32:04,023 --> 00:32:06,125
Are you done yet?
No, I'm not done yet.

716
00:32:06,125 --> 00:32:08,293
Okay, let's do a fly by
at that nudist colony.

717
00:32:08,293 --> 00:32:10,297
Swinging into high
Jedi, I feel the need,

718
00:32:10,297 --> 00:32:11,597
the need for speed.

719
00:32:11,597 --> 00:32:13,767
Come on, Servo.
Who?

720
00:32:13,767 --> 00:32:15,335
I mean Commando Servo.

721
00:32:15,335 --> 00:32:17,903
I think Crow wants
to talk to us.

722
00:32:17,903 --> 00:32:19,238
You're a good little helper Ted.

723
00:32:19,238 --> 00:32:20,740
Let's go, come on.

724
00:32:20,740 --> 00:32:23,542
- Hey, you guy,
I mean earth man.

725
00:32:23,542 --> 00:32:26,578
I want you to take an atomic
bomb the size of a pineapple,

726
00:32:26,578 --> 00:32:31,150
strap it to a Piper Cub and
then crash into Mount Vesuvius.

727
00:32:31,150 --> 00:32:32,485
Then on your way back,

728
00:32:32,485 --> 00:32:34,920
swing by Al's and pick
me up a Swiss cheese

729
00:32:34,920 --> 00:32:37,090
on a college of roll.

730
00:32:37,090 --> 00:32:38,490
I can't get into this.

731
00:32:38,490 --> 00:32:41,027
Joel, I wanna be commander
Cody for a while.

732
00:32:41,027 --> 00:32:42,562
- Ted, who is that
squeaky little worm

733
00:32:42,562 --> 00:32:43,830
in the caftan down there?

734
00:32:43,830 --> 00:32:46,332
- It's Crog and he wants
to wear your costume.

735
00:32:46,332 --> 00:32:48,300
- Does he have any idea
who he is dealing with?

736
00:32:48,300 --> 00:32:49,768
I couldn't...

737
00:32:49,768 --> 00:32:51,270
- Yeah, you're Servo out
when Joel's holding you up.

738
00:32:51,270 --> 00:32:53,172
- Pay no attention to
the man holding me up.

739
00:32:53,172 --> 00:32:54,740
Take me down to
Ted, I'm on a roll.

740
00:32:54,740 --> 00:32:57,010
- Oh come on Servo,
don't be such a baby.

741
00:32:57,010 --> 00:32:58,543
- Alright, Crow, the jig is up.

742
00:32:58,543 --> 00:33:00,447
- Put on the cheese pistol
and fight me like a man.

743
00:33:00,447 --> 00:33:02,282
- I'll jam it in your
centuri bubble head.

744
00:33:02,282 --> 00:33:03,248
Come on, give me that cut.

745
00:33:03,248 --> 00:33:04,283
Lets go moon man, let's gone.

746
00:33:04,283 --> 00:33:06,252
- Saved my commercial sign.

747
00:33:06,252 --> 00:33:08,020
- You're lucky my chick's here.

748
00:33:08,020 --> 00:33:10,590
(upbeat music)

749
00:33:19,965 --> 00:33:21,467
- [Tom] Fly me in Ted.

750
00:33:21,467 --> 00:33:25,738
- [Joel] No, next time Crow
gets to be Commando Cody.

751
00:33:25,738 --> 00:33:26,538
- [Crow] Did you hear that?

752
00:33:26,538 --> 00:33:27,707
He said I could do it.

753
00:33:27,707 --> 00:33:30,943
- [Tom] Commando
Crow will never work.

754
00:33:30,943 --> 00:33:33,212
You're too much of a pansy.

755
00:33:34,213 --> 00:33:36,215
- [Crow] That's it.

756
00:33:36,215 --> 00:33:37,050
That's it.

757
00:33:39,685 --> 00:33:41,453
I don't know what
it is, but it's it.

758
00:33:41,453 --> 00:33:43,555
- [Joel] Robert Heinlein.

759
00:33:47,493 --> 00:33:51,697
- Hey, get me fellows,
I'm playing the violin.

760
00:33:51,697 --> 00:33:56,068
- [Crow] Jerome Pycha jr.
cousin of Jerome Elite.

761
00:33:56,068 --> 00:33:57,903
Kind of a typist joke.

762
00:33:59,938 --> 00:34:02,142
- [Joel] Miniatures by Jacque...

763
00:34:02,142 --> 00:34:03,943
What do they have
miniatures for?

764
00:34:03,943 --> 00:34:05,578
- [Crow] They used a
lot of Hummel figurines

765
