1255
00:53:06,317 --> 00:53:08,220
Now what am I to tell him?

1256
00:53:08,220 --> 00:53:11,088
(Crow mumbling)

1257
00:53:11,088 --> 00:53:13,190
- This round of the moon
flight is a necessary step

1258
00:53:13,190 --> 00:53:14,993
before establishing
a base on the moon.

1259
00:53:14,993 --> 00:53:16,728
It's a survey flight.

1260
00:53:17,595 --> 00:53:18,530
- Maybe someday the statesman--

1261
00:53:18,530 --> 00:53:20,032
- [Joel] He's so military,

1262
00:53:20,032 --> 00:53:22,233
I thought he gives
good spankings.

1263
00:53:22,233 --> 00:53:23,935
- It's so fine but
in the meantime,

1264
00:53:23,935 --> 00:53:26,605
if there is going to
be a base on the moon

1265
00:53:26,605 --> 00:53:28,907
and there will be--

1266
00:53:28,907 --> 00:53:32,277
- [Tom] I wanted
to be first place.

1267
00:53:32,277 --> 00:53:34,712
- [Joel] I'm not even
supposed to be here.

1268
00:53:34,712 --> 00:53:37,448
- Ma'am, the most important
thing in the world to me

1269
00:53:37,448 --> 00:53:40,285
is the military security
of the United States.

1270
00:53:40,285 --> 00:53:41,787
- [Crow] And my dog Flappy.

1271
00:53:41,787 --> 00:53:44,688
- And I'm not in the least bit
apologetic for my attitude.

1272
00:53:44,688 --> 00:53:45,757
- I wonder general,

1273
00:53:45,757 --> 00:53:46,925
could you tell me something

1274
00:53:46,925 --> 00:53:48,125
about this wonderful
space station.

1275
00:53:48,125 --> 00:53:49,427
- [Joel] I'll help you
with the cue cards.

1276
00:53:49,427 --> 00:53:51,295
- That will be very
interesting general.

1277
00:53:51,295 --> 00:53:53,498
- Well, I can give
you a rough idea.

1278
00:53:53,498 --> 00:53:57,635
The station is a titanium
hole, with steel bracing,

1279
00:53:57,635 --> 00:53:59,370
350 feet in diameter.

1280
00:54:01,973 --> 00:54:03,240
It rotates completely
around the earth

1281
00:54:03,240 --> 00:54:06,978
in a trans-polar orbit,
about 10 times a day.

1282
00:54:09,147 --> 00:54:11,215
At present the station is
in a state of free fall.

1283
00:54:11,215 --> 00:54:13,952
- Free fall, could you explain
that a little bit more.

1284
00:54:13,952 --> 00:54:15,387
- Off course, when we
speak to free fall,

1285
00:54:15,387 --> 00:54:18,055
we simply mean that the
station and everything in it,

1286
00:54:18,055 --> 00:54:20,025
are moving around the earth

1287
00:54:20,025 --> 00:54:22,893
at a speed which is
great enough so that

1288
00:54:22,893 --> 00:54:25,297
it cannot fall toward the earth,

1289
00:54:25,297 --> 00:54:28,833
but it is also
moving at the speed,

1290
00:54:28,833 --> 00:54:30,968
which is not great enough

1291
00:54:30,968 --> 00:54:34,038
in order to enable it
to go out into space.

1292
00:54:34,038 --> 00:54:34,872
Therefore,

1293
00:54:36,340 --> 00:54:39,477
the forces of gravity and
speed are now in balance.

1294
00:54:39,477 --> 00:54:40,678
(Joel sighs)

1295
00:54:40,678 --> 00:54:41,813
- [Joel] That was very good.

1296
00:54:41,813 --> 00:54:43,213
Yeah.

1297
00:54:43,213 --> 00:54:45,450
Nothing in the station
has any weight.

1298
00:54:45,450 --> 00:54:48,820
- No, wait, what
a wonderful idea!

1299
00:54:48,820 --> 00:54:51,622
You mean if I went I
wouldn't wear anything.

1300
00:54:51,622 --> 00:54:53,358
- Nothing at all.

1301
00:54:53,358 --> 00:54:54,825
As a matter of fact,

1302
00:54:54,825 --> 00:54:56,695
you'd have to wear magnetic
shoes to keep you on the floor.

1303
00:54:56,695 --> 00:55:00,398
- [Crow] Well, I have a
pink out of those at home.

1304
00:55:00,398 --> 00:55:01,833
- I wondered general,

1305
00:55:01,833 --> 00:55:05,070
could I arrange to go
there, to the space station?

1306
00:55:05,070 --> 00:55:07,038
- Well, hardly Ms. Prettles.

1307
00:55:07,038 --> 00:55:08,038
- [Joel] There's
the little problem

1308
00:55:08,038 --> 00:55:10,308
of escape philosophy ma'am.

1309
00:55:10,308 --> 00:55:15,180
- It's about $300 a pound to
send anything to the station.

1310
00:55:15,180 --> 00:55:16,613
And consequently,

1311
00:55:16,613 --> 00:55:19,183
our personnel almost always
less than 160 pounds.

1312
00:55:19,183 --> 00:55:21,185
- [Joel] You're over
by a metric tone.

1313
00:55:21,185 --> 00:55:23,788
- It is so lovely to
weigh nothing at all.

1314
00:55:23,788 --> 00:55:25,190
(laughing)

1315
00:55:25,190 --> 00:55:26,958
- I've heard of
the H bomb General.

1316
00:55:26,958 --> 00:55:30,028
Isn't it dangerous living
and working so near to it.

1317
00:55:30,028 --> 00:55:31,528
- I'm very sorry doctor,

1318
00:55:31,528 --> 00:55:33,665
but that's a highly
classified subject.

1319
00:55:33,665 --> 00:55:37,468
- [Crow] A simple yes
or no would do dickweed.

1320
00:55:41,840 --> 00:55:43,408
- [Joel] Isn't she something?

1321
00:55:43,408 --> 00:55:45,843
- [Crow] Yeah and the
girl ain't bad either.

1322
00:55:45,843 --> 00:55:49,380
- General Green, your rocket
ship number three editor,

1323
00:55:49,380 --> 00:55:51,448
ready for takeoff
to space station.

1324
00:55:51,448 --> 00:55:53,485
- [Joel] No diving
or splashing please.

1325
00:55:53,485 --> 00:55:54,985
And no running on the deck.

1326
00:55:54,985 --> 00:55:56,253
- Happy landing, sir.

1327
00:55:56,253 --> 00:55:58,390
- Colonel Breteis,
your ship is zero.

1328
00:55:58,390 --> 00:56:00,192
Check off list completed.

1329
00:56:00,192 --> 00:56:01,458
- Do you need any help?

1330
00:56:01,458 --> 00:56:02,893
- No thank you Major,

1331
00:56:02,893 --> 00:56:06,097
I'm perfectly capable of
getting into the rocket myself

1332
00:56:06,097 --> 00:56:09,700
- [Joel] Well all right,
Ms. Gloria Steinem.

1333
00:56:11,435 --> 00:56:12,737
- [Tom] That's Miss
Glorious Steinem.

1334
00:56:12,737 --> 00:56:14,438
- [Joel] Aright yeah.

1335
00:56:15,907 --> 00:56:17,508
- [Tom] Hey, and
there's only one bunk.

1336
00:56:17,508 --> 00:56:19,010
- May I strap you in colonel.

1337
00:56:19,010 --> 00:56:20,645
- No, thank you major.

1338
00:56:20,645 --> 00:56:21,913
Are your ship to ship

1339
00:56:21,913 --> 00:56:24,182
and ship to blockhouse
frequencies operating?

1340
00:56:24,182 --> 00:56:25,650
- Incoming only colonel.

1341
00:56:25,650 --> 00:56:27,985
- Orders are to keep
the channels clear

1342
00:56:27,985 --> 00:56:30,088
until the Canada blast off.

1343
00:56:30,088 --> 00:56:31,422
- Canada to blockhouse,

1344
00:56:31,422 --> 00:56:34,158
request permission
to start pumps.

1345
00:56:34,158 --> 00:56:36,995
- [Crow] Sorry yeah,
but Canada is dry.

1346
00:56:36,995 --> 00:56:38,863
- Request permission
to blast off.

1347
00:56:38,863 --> 00:56:40,132
- Permission granted.

1348
00:56:40,132 --> 00:56:42,267
- [Crow] Hey Canada,
take off your hoses.

1349
00:56:42,267 --> 00:56:46,437
- [Joel] Yeah our subject
today is space launches.

1350
00:56:47,938 --> 00:56:50,742
So we're gonna have a takeoff.

1351
00:56:50,742 --> 00:56:52,210
Hey, you get it?

1352
00:56:52,210 --> 00:56:53,745
You know it's kinda like a
rocket it's going to take off

1353
00:56:53,745 --> 00:56:57,015
and then they say
take off on that bit.

1354
00:56:58,382 --> 00:56:59,617
- [Crow] Look at that take off.

1355
00:56:59,617 --> 00:57:00,818
- [Joel] Well good
day to you then.

1356
00:57:00,818 --> 00:57:03,488
(rocket flying)

1357
00:57:14,998 --> 00:57:18,135
- You may start blast
off procedure captain.

1358
00:57:18,135 --> 00:57:19,803
- Thank you colonel.

1359
00:57:21,305 --> 00:57:22,707
- Mexico to blockhouse,

1360
00:57:22,707 --> 00:57:26,043
request permission
to start pumps.

1361
00:57:26,043 --> 00:57:27,812
- Permission granted.

1362
00:57:29,380 --> 00:57:30,648
- Mexico to blockhouse.

1363
00:57:30,648 --> 00:57:33,518
- [Crow] Make a
run for the border.

1364
00:57:33,518 --> 00:57:36,822
- Blockhouse to Mexico,
clearance granted.

1365
00:57:36,822 --> 00:57:38,523
You are minus 10 seconds.

1366
00:57:38,523 --> 00:57:39,790
Nine,

1367
00:57:39,790 --> 00:57:40,725
eight.

1368
00:57:40,725 --> 00:57:41,792
- [Tom] Three.
- Seven.

1369
00:57:41,792 --> 00:57:42,660
- [Tom] 13.

1370
00:57:42,660 --> 00:57:43,628
- Six.
- [Joel] nine.

1371
00:57:43,628 --> 00:57:45,028
- Five.
[Tom] 128.

1372
00:57:45,028 --> 00:57:46,497
- Four.
- [Tom] 33.

1373
00:57:46,497 --> 00:57:47,732
- 1,000,005.

1374
00:57:47,732 --> 00:57:49,200
- Two, one.

1375
00:57:49,200 --> 00:57:52,670
- [Joel] Don't blow
it, it's a big trunk.

1376
00:57:59,043 --> 00:58:01,212
Buddy absence's happy.

1377
00:58:01,212 --> 00:58:03,948
(people yelling)

1378
00:58:05,148 --> 00:58:08,085
- [Tom] She's
absolutely ballistic.

1379
00:58:09,920 --> 00:58:12,690
(dramatic music)

1380
00:58:15,860 --> 00:58:17,695
- Base control to Mexico.

1381
00:58:17,695 --> 00:58:19,563
Prepare to receive line.

1382
00:58:19,563 --> 00:58:22,800
- [Tom] It looks like
Deep 13 kind off.

1383
00:58:27,238 --> 00:58:30,442
- Turn to lock
free, bring them in.

1384
00:58:30,442 --> 00:58:33,210
(dramatic music)

1385
00:58:37,415 --> 00:58:39,983
- [Tom] Welcome to wammo world.

1386
00:58:54,498 --> 00:58:56,433
- [Joel] That ought to do it.

1387
00:58:56,433 --> 00:58:59,970
- Lock three to Mexico,
you are secured.

1388
00:58:59,970 --> 00:59:01,973
You may disembark, over.

1389
00:59:04,375 --> 00:59:06,945
- Mexico to lock
three disembarking.

1390
00:59:06,945 --> 00:59:09,713
(people barking)

1391
00:59:15,018 --> 00:59:16,753
I must report immediately.

1392
00:59:16,753 --> 00:59:18,555
See you before you leave.

1393
00:59:18,555 --> 00:59:20,525
I'll be with you as
far as weight control.

1394
00:59:20,525 --> 00:59:21,458
- [Joel] I don't need
any weight control,

1395
00:59:21,458 --> 00:59:24,095
maybe a tummy tuck or something.

1396
00:59:24,095 --> 00:59:25,597
- [Tom] This is all muscle.

1397
00:59:25,597 --> 00:59:28,365
(dramatic music)

1398
00:59:33,303 --> 00:59:35,473
- [Announcer] Simon winds up.

1399
00:59:35,473 --> 00:59:36,907
And it's a pitch.

1400
00:59:38,075 --> 00:59:39,977
And it's a home
run for Brooklyn.

1401
00:59:39,977 --> 00:59:42,080
- Back to business major.

1402
00:59:42,080 --> 00:59:43,480
- [Crow] This is the future

1403
00:59:43,480 --> 00:59:45,883
when they sold the
Dodgers back to Brooklyn.

1404
00:59:45,883 --> 00:59:48,118
- Hope you enjoyed
the trip colonel.

1405
00:59:48,118 --> 00:59:49,453
Happy landings Bill.

1406
00:59:49,453 --> 00:59:50,722
- Thank you Captain.

1407
00:59:50,722 --> 00:59:52,623
- [Joel] Oh, you dropped
your pen, shoe's untied.

1408
00:59:52,623 --> 00:59:53,457
(Joel laughs)

1409
00:59:53,457 --> 00:59:54,425
I love this.

1410
00:59:55,560 --> 00:59:57,528
- [Crow] Hey, don't
cross the split screen.

1411
00:59:57,528 --> 01:00:00,432
- [Joel] Art designed
by MC Escher.

1412
01:00:05,703 --> 01:00:06,972
- Please be seated.

1413
01:00:06,972 --> 01:00:08,172
- Thank you, sir.

1414
01:00:08,172 --> 01:00:10,642
- Nice to see you
again colonel, major.

1415
01:00:10,642 --> 01:00:11,475
- [Crow] Major.

1416
01:00:11,475 --> 01:00:12,310
- [Joel] Colonel.

1417
01:00:12,310 --> 01:00:13,845
- [Crow] Doctor.

1418
01:00:13,845 --> 01:00:14,978
Captain.

1419
01:00:14,978 --> 01:00:16,647
You're in free fall.

1420
01:00:18,983 --> 01:00:20,952
- The General's
asked me to brief you

1421
01:00:20,952 --> 01:00:23,053
on the conditions of this shoot.

1422
01:00:23,053 --> 01:00:26,223
As you know, it's to be
a circumlunar flight.

1423
01:00:26,223 --> 01:00:27,925
Colonel Breteis will pilot,

1424
01:00:27,925 --> 01:00:29,960
major Moore co-pilot.

1425
01:00:29,960 --> 01:00:32,730
Doctor Werhner will do the
photographic and scientific work

1426
01:00:32,730 --> 01:00:35,198
as you pass around the
back face of the moon.

1427
01:00:35,198 --> 01:00:36,933
- I think we should
attempt a landing sir.

1428
01:00:36,933 --> 01:00:39,470
- [Joel] Shut up.
- One step at a time colonel.

1429
01:00:39,470 --> 01:00:41,505
There'll be only a 25
second margin of fuel,

1430
01:00:41,505 --> 01:00:43,742
open above that calculator that
is necessary for the flight

1431
01:00:43,742 --> 01:00:46,543
and resumption of the
orbit for the station.

1432
01:00:46,543 --> 01:00:48,212
Therefore, you must
proceed exactly

1433
01:00:48,212 --> 01:00:50,147
according to your flight plan.

1434
01:00:50,147 --> 01:00:52,083
If you make this one all right,

1435
01:00:52,083 --> 01:00:55,218
we may give you a crack
at the first moon landing.

1436
01:00:55,218 --> 01:00:56,753
- [Joel] Breteis for 50 points.

1437
01:00:56,753 --> 01:00:59,290
- The Magellan is fueled
and ready according to plan.

1438
01:00:59,290 --> 01:01:01,058
Check off list completed.

1439
01:01:01,058 --> 01:01:02,293
- [Joel] Bill for 20 points.

1440
01:01:02,293 --> 01:01:05,397
- You'll burst
off in 37 minutes.

1441
01:01:05,397 --> 01:01:06,830
It's yours colonel.

1442
01:01:06,830 --> 01:01:08,032
Man Your ship.

1443
01:01:08,032 --> 01:01:09,700
- [Crow] Or woman
your ship as it were.

1444
01:01:09,700 --> 01:01:12,203
(Crow laughs)

1445
01:01:13,670 --> 01:01:17,975
- [Joel] Boy, walking on the
walls must be a big problem.

1446
01:01:22,880 --> 01:01:25,215
- [Tom] Speed bump.

1447
01:01:25,215 --> 01:01:27,952
(dramatic music)

1448
01:01:29,820 --> 01:01:32,890
- Magellan to lock four,
all secure shove off.

1449
01:01:32,890 --> 01:01:33,725
- [Tom] Same to you tuts.

1450
01:01:33,725 --> 01:01:35,158
- Lock four to Magellan.

1451
01:01:35,158 --> 01:01:38,295
Shoving off on count of ten.

1452
01:01:38,295 --> 01:01:41,865
- [Crow] The technical
term of shoving off.

1453
01:01:50,173 --> 01:01:51,808
- [Breteis] Magellan
to space control.

1454
01:01:51,808 --> 01:01:54,212
Check starting
coordinates, over.

1455
01:01:54,212 --> 01:01:58,582
- Your coordinates of polaris
83 degrees, 62 minutes,

1456
01:01:58,715 --> 01:02:04,555
max's A, regulars 180
degrees, 29 minutes.

1457
01:02:04,922 --> 01:02:06,523
max's B, clomohog--

1458
01:02:07,392 --> 01:02:09,193
- [Joel] (mumbling).

1459
01:02:09,193 --> 01:02:12,630
Radius, meaningless
dribble, over.

1460
01:02:12,630 --> 01:02:15,065
- [Tom] Initiate cheesy
effects sequence.

1461
01:02:15,065 --> 01:02:19,003
- [Crow] Roger that,
initiating cheesy FX pill.

1462
01:02:20,403 --> 01:02:23,373
- [Joel] Look they're using
View-Master technology.

1463
01:02:23,373 --> 01:02:25,777
- [Tom] Battery pack
separating from Frisbee.

1464
01:02:25,777 --> 01:02:28,512
(dramatic music)

1465
01:02:35,920 --> 01:02:37,155
- [Joel] Look the Grand Tetons.

1466
01:02:37,155 --> 01:02:40,423
- Swing slowly right
about two degree.

1467
01:02:40,423 --> 01:02:42,160
No south, one degree.

1468
01:02:43,427 --> 01:02:44,762
Little more down.

1469
01:02:44,762 --> 01:02:45,597
Hold it.

1470
01:02:46,563 --> 01:02:47,798
- [Tom] Perfect.

1471
01:02:47,798 --> 01:02:50,400
(loud beeping)

1472
01:03:00,443 --> 01:03:02,847
- [Breteis] Steady.

1473
01:03:02,980 --> 01:03:04,982
Hold it.

1474
01:03:05,115 --> 01:03:08,618
- [Joel] Handling the Indian
ceremony at the grand Canyon.

1475
01:03:08,618 --> 01:03:10,287
- Rocketship Magellan
to space control.

1476
01:03:10,287 --> 01:03:13,223
We are now correctly
aligned, over.

1477
01:03:15,727 --> 01:03:18,830
- You have 13
seconds to blast off.

1478
01:03:18,830 --> 01:03:20,397
Mark,

1479
01:03:20,397 --> 01:03:21,232
13,

1480
01:03:22,200 --> 01:03:23,800
12,

1481
01:03:23,800 --> 01:03:25,368
11,

1482
01:03:25,368 --> 01:03:26,337
10,

1483
01:03:26,337 --> 01:03:27,472
nine,

1484
01:03:27,472 --> 01:03:28,638
eight,

1485
01:03:28,638 --> 01:03:29,907
seven,

1486
01:03:29,907 --> 01:03:31,042
six,

1487
01:03:31,042 --> 01:03:32,443
five

1488
01:03:32,443 --> 01:03:33,710
four,

1489
01:03:33,710 --> 01:03:35,012
three,

1490
01:03:35,012 --> 01:03:36,047
two,

1491
01:03:36,047 --> 01:03:37,248
one,

1492
01:03:37,248 --> 01:03:38,615
fire.

1493
01:03:38,615 --> 01:03:40,685
- [Crow] Wow, free game.

1494
01:03:40,685 --> 01:03:44,388
- [Joel] Duracell away
the copper top shuttle.

1495
01:03:44,388 --> 01:03:47,157
(dramatic music)

1496
01:03:52,028 --> 01:03:53,030
- [Tom] Bye.

1497
01:03:54,298 --> 01:03:55,198
Bon voyage.

1498
01:03:59,437 --> 01:04:02,707
- [Joel] Numbers are really
meaningless in a gravitometer.

1499
01:04:02,707 --> 01:04:05,777
- [Crow] Initiate
meaningless lights.

1500
01:04:08,045 --> 01:04:09,980
- [Tom] And up it goes.

1501
01:04:15,285 --> 01:04:17,855
(upbeat music)

1502
01:04:22,927 --> 01:04:25,697
- But what is
controlling the ship now?

1503
01:04:25,697 --> 01:04:27,665
- As you can see by the
lights and the tape control,

1504
01:04:27,665 --> 01:04:30,367
the autopilot is keeping
us on our computer track

1505
01:04:30,367 --> 01:04:33,003
with the ship and
its proper attitude.

